WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.000
AI red teaming is a structured effort to identify weaknesses, misuse risks, and failure modes in AI systems.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:15.220
It helps organizations understand how systems behave under pressure, unexpected inputs, adversarial conditions, or risky workflows.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.200
The goal is not to show off clever prompts or break systems for entertainment.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:25.740
The goal is to discover problems early so teams can reduce harm, improve controls, and make better risk decisions.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:31.400
Responsible AI red teaming is authorized, scoped, documented, and tied to remediation.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:38.820
It should help builders, security teams, product owners, and governance teams understand what can go wrong and how to reduce the likelihood or impact.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.480
A useful assessment treats the AI system as a complete product.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:52.140
The model matters, but so do prompts, retrieval, tools, data, permissions, logs, workflows, user experience, and operating procedures.
